  "body": "## What\n\n- Resolve all Chevrotain `lodash-es` lockfile edges to the existing patched 4.18.1 package.\n- Add passing, failing, and bounded use case parser fixtures.\n- Record the dependency chain, source trace, Dependabot failure, validation, and post-merge alert check in the evidence report.\n\n## Why\n\nMermaid 12.0.0 pulls Chevrotain 11.1.2, which pins `lodash-es` 4.17.23 exactly. The lockfile repair removes the version flagged by alerts #1 and #2 while keeping the direct Mermaid and jsdom pins unchanged. A future fresh resolution should be checked because Chevrotain still declares 4.17.23.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- [Committed evidence report](https://github.com/tbhb/agent-orchestration-poc/blob/f34e826/reports/inputs/lodash-es-alert-evidence.md)\n- `pnpm why lodash-es` shows one version, 4.18.1, after the frozen install.\n- `mise run check:mermaid`, `mise run check`, `mise run check:mutation`, and `mise run build` passed locally. The intentionally invalid fixture failed as expected.\n- Harness: Codex CLI 0.157.1. Model: `gpt-6-sol` at medium effort.\n- Diff size: 107 changed lines across five files, including 11 lockfile lines, 80 report lines, and 16 fixture lines. Counted code lines: 0.\n\n## Docs\n\nThe evidence report records the exposure conclusion. No direct dependency pin moved, so the docs stack and tooling conventions did not need an update. The coordinator will check alert closure after merge and link that result on issue #102.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] CI green\n- [x] Docs updated or not required\n- [x] No secrets in committed evidence\n- [x] Evidence committed\n\nRefs: #102\n",
